--- README.md ---
Two plots share the numerical renderer. The ribbon shows measured samples and the overlay shows simulated samples. The final displayed point is the mean of a trailing window.

--- settings.py ---
SERIES_SPAN = 1
TRACE_SPAN = 4

--- app.py ---
import settings

STREAM = {"ribbon": "probe", "overlay": "model"}
WINDOWS = {"probe": settings.SERIES_SPAN, "model": settings.TRACE_SPAN}

def final_point(plot, samples):
    window = samples[-WINDOWS[STREAM[plot]]:]
    return sum(window) / len(window)

